Streamripper 1.65.0-rc.1 validation
=================================

Date: 2026-10-20
Local platform: Debian 13, Linux x86_64
Toolchain: Clang 19.1.7, CMake 3.31.6, Ninja 1.12.1
Libraries: GLib 2.84.4, curl 8.14.1, libmad 0.15.1b,
           libogg 1.3.5, libvorbis 1.3.7
Independent decoder used during validation: FFmpeg/ffprobe 7.1.5.

Reproducible offline checks
---------------------------

  make test
  make release
  make lint
  cmake --preset thread
  cmake --build --preset thread
  ctest --preset thread

All builds treat compiler and linker warnings as errors. The strict profile
uses AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer without suppression files;
the thread profile uses ThreadSanitizer. Static analysis covers every compiled
translation unit with Clang's core, dead-code and POSIX analyzer groups.
ShellCheck covers the station helper and fixture regeneration script.

CTest's core suite checks:
  - PLS/M3U and embedded station URL resolution, including relative URLs.
  - UTF-8, Windows-1252 fallback, malformed UTF-8, byte-limited copies,
    UTF-16 BOMs and complete surrogate pairs.
  - Both MP3 splitters against a synthetic stereo signal whose channels have
    opposite phase, with a known two-second silent gap; uninterrupted mono
    audio must fall back near the search-window center.
  - Padding bounds, corrupt MP3 data, ADTS boundaries, circular-buffer
    offsets, bounded relay headers and case-insensitive AAC/ICY headers.

CTest's integration suite starts local HTTP and certificate-backed HTTPS
servers. It checks actual libcurl reads, fragmented/chunked data with trailers,
compression, relative redirects, PLS/M3U, TLS trust and rejection, redirect and
playlist cycles, missing resources, stalls, unsupported HLS/JSON, and excessive
ICY metadata intervals. It also checks shutdown before the first audio bytes.
A bounded burst with a valid 45000-byte ICY interval must reach the track file
without waiting for the historical 24-block startup buffer to fill.

The complete CLI records synthetic MP3 with both splitters (including overlap
padding), ADTS AAC, and Ogg/Vorbis. Completed MP3/AAC tracks are walked frame by
frame to prove that their boundaries contain no lost or partial frames. UTF-8
filenames, UTF-16 ID3v2.3 values, Latin-1 ID3v1 tags and unusually long metadata
are inspected. Long titles exercise dynamically sized ID3 headers and filename
version collisions. ICY blocks deliberately contain no NUL terminator and use
length bytes above 127. Unsupported Ogg/Opus is rejected with a nonzero status.
All audio fixtures are generated from mathematical tones, not recordings.

