Practical limits
----------------

This is a release candidate. Live availability, geo restrictions and station
page schemas may change. Split-point detection remains heuristic, especially
for crossfades, continuous progressive music and delayed title announcements.
The first captured MP3 frame may depend on an earlier bit reservoir; dropping
the first partial track is the default. Stopping can omit final buffered audio.
Use continuous show recording when retaining the whole programme is essential.
No multi-day endurance or universal codec compatibility is claimed.

HLS/DASH, DRM, Opus, arbitrary HTML players and the historical Windows/Winamp
projects are outside the validated release scope. Unsupported detected formats
produce an error. AAC splitting aligns ADTS frames and does not analyze silence.
The release tarball requires compatible system GLib, curl, Ogg/Vorbis and libc;
libmad is linked statically. See README for build and recording commands.
